note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note This file is a specification illustration. It uses record declarations,
note abilities and control flow, which the single file reference front end does
note not implement yet (see spec/15 section 15.8). Programs that the reference
note can compile today are hello.shark, tour*.shark, pages.shark and ambiguity.shark.
note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

note A small game. Shows records, handlers, regions, parallel data work and
note zero-allocation frames. Every memory decision here is made by the compiler.

use draw2d
use physics
use input

a player has
  position as a point
  velocity as a point
  health as a whole number starting at 100

a particle has
  position as a point
  velocity as a point
  life as a decimal number

keep hero as a player with
  position as a point with x as 0 and y as 0
  velocity as a point with x as 0 and y as 0

keep enemies as empty list
keep sparks as empty list

page Game
  scrolling
    show text Health value of health of hero

  when Start is pressed
    open page Game

note --------------------------------------------------------------- gameplay

to spawn a burst at a place
  repeat 200 times
    add a particle with
      position as place
      velocity as random direction times 4
      life as 1
    to sparks

to damage a target by an amount
  set health of target to health of target minus amount
  if health of target is at most 0
    open page Game Over

when hero touches an enemy
  damage hero by 10
  spawn a burst at position of hero

when the world updates
  during this frame
    keep visible as empty list

    for each p in sparks at the same time
      set position of p to position of p plus velocity of p
      set life of p to life of p minus 0.016

    for each p in sparks
      if life of p is more than 0
        add p to visible

    for each p in visible
      draw a circle
        at position of p
        with radius 2
        filled with white fading by life of p

  remove dead sparks from sparks

when the player presses jump
  set velocity of hero to velocity of hero plus a point with x as 0 and y as 9

page Game Over
  centred
    in a column spaced 16
      show text Game over
      show button Try again to page Game

note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note What the compiler decides here, viewable with `compose explain storage`:
note
note   hero            module state, unique heap, one owner
note   sparks backing  unique heap, grown in place
note   visible backing REGION `this frame`, freed in one operation
note   p in the loops  borrowed from `this frame`, never copied
note   the point maths registers, scalar replaced, never materialised
note
note Net heap allocations per frame: zero.
note The `for each ... at the same time` loop vectorises to 8 lanes on AVX2
note because the compiler has already proved the sparks list is not aliased.
